  "findings": [
    "The standalone FactorySequenceNote{,Across,OverSeveral}Command END grammar accepts end plus zero/one %s plus any of note/hnote/rnote, independent of opener; attached FactorySequenceNoteOnArrowCommand permits only note. Pattern2 transforms %s to Java ASCII \\s plus NBSP and compiles with CASE_INSENSITIVE only. Rust correctly separates attached ownership but its new Unicode \\s broadens this grammar.",
    "Introduced rejection-contract losses: indf535_terminator_em_space_{legacy,teoz} and indf535_terminator_narrow_nbsp_{legacy,teoz}. All four immutable intended-invalid inputs produce Java error SVGs, exit200 and nonempty stderr. Before CLI rejects with exit1/Unclosed sequence note; after CLI succeeds with exit0 and consumes the invalid end-rnote line. This is a regression caused by 61e6aeed6, not a pre-existing residual. Comparator invalid-reference status2 must not conceal the four lost rejection passes.",
    "The NBSP controls are Java-valid and recover from parser error to full match. Case variants, tab, no-gap spelling, surrounding spaces, mismatched legal terminators and nested-looking note text follow the intended grammar in fresh controls. Double internal spaces, extra suffix and attached end-rnote remain rejections, with all negative intents preserved.",
    "Fresh28 includes18 positive references and10 negatives. Fourteen positive outputs match; four whole failures remain on adjacent mixed-shape notes inside groups and uppercase attached hexagonal self notes, both engines. Before had two matches and16 valid parse errors; after has no valid parse error. The four new invalid-input false accepts plus residual whole failures reject this mechanism."
